  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDA17 Core Grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Development Association (IDA) is an international financial institution which offers concessional loans and grants to the world&apos;s poorest developing countries. The IDA is a member of the World Bank Group and complements the existing the existing International Bank for Reconstruction and Development by lending to developing countries which suffer from the lowest gross national income, from troubled creditworthiness, or from the lowest per capita income. Funding under this initiative represents the Core Grant component (17%) of Australia&apos;s contribution to IDA17. The total value of our IDA17 core contribution is $582.8 million to be expensed over the period 10 June 2014 to 30 June 2023.</narrative>
  </description>
